Through the usage of the foreign_enum! macro you can "export" enums (C like enum) to a foreign language: #[derive(Clone, Copy)]
enum MyEnum { Item1, Item2, Item3,
} foreign_enum!( enum MyEnum { ITEM1 = MyEnum::Item1, ITEM2 = MyEnum::Item2, ITEM3 = MyEnum::Item3, }
); This allows you to use it as input or output types for foreign_class! methods.

